      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "informationUri": "https://turion-platform-drift",
          "name": "turion-platform-drift",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "TPD001",
              "name": "boto3/botocoreSDKimport",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "boto3 / botocore SDK import"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Ground-service code imports the proprietary AWS SDK directly, so the module cannot be imported on a non-AWS ground station."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Replace with the portable ground-station storage interface (any S3-compatible endpoint: MinIO, VersityGW) and read ARNs from environment configuration.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** OpenC3-compatible object-store shim + typed config\n\nReplace with the portable ground-station storage interface (any S3-compatible endpoint: MinIO, VersityGW) and read ARNs from environment configuration."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "compute",
                "portability": "OpenC3-compatible object-store shim + typed config",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD002",
              "name": "boto3clientboundtoaproprietaryAWSservice",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "boto3 client bound to a proprietary AWS service"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A boto3 client is constructed for an AWS-only service (batch, lambda, s3, dynamodb, sqs, sns, ...), hard-coding the proprietary control plane."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Route the call through the portability interface; Batch becomes a Kubernetes Job, Lambda becomes a Deployment/Job, DynamoDB becomes PostgreSQL/Postgres-compatible, SQS/SNS becomes NATS/Redpanda.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** Kubernetes Job / Crossplane composite\n\nRoute the call through the portability interface; Batch becomes a Kubernetes Job, Lambda becomes a Deployment/Job, DynamoDB becomes PostgreSQL/Postgres-compatible, SQS/SNS becomes NATS/Redpanda."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "compute",
                "portability": "Kubernetes Job / Crossplane composite",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD003",
              "name": "AWSLambdainvocation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AWS Lambda invocation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Code invokes a Lambda function, which cannot exist in an air-gapped or on-premises ground station."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Deploy the function body as a Kubernetes Job/Deployment and call it over HTTP (or the Knative Serving route) instead of Invoke.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** Kubernetes Job + ClusterIP Service\n\nDeploy the function body as a Kubernetes Job/Deployment and call it over HTTP (or the Knative Serving route) instead of Invoke."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "serverless",
                "portability": "Kubernetes Job + ClusterIP Service",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD004",
              "name": "AWSBatchjobsubmission",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AWS Batch job submission"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Code or manifests submit to AWS Batch (submit_job, jobQueue, jobDefinition), which has no portable equivalent unless re-hosted."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Generate a Kubernetes Job (with backoffLimit and ttlSecondsAfterFinished) from the Batch job definition.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** Kubernetes Job manifest\n\nGenerate a Kubernetes Job (with backoffLimit and ttlSecondsAfterFinished) from the Batch job definition."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "compute",
                "portability": "Kubernetes Job manifest",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD005",
              "name": "Hard-codedS3bucket/ARNliteral",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded S3 bucket / ARN literal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A bucket name or arn:aws:s3 ARN is embedded in source, binding the deployment to one AWS account and region."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Read the endpoint, bucket, and credentials from a ConfigMap/Secret; point them at MinIO or VersityGW.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** MinIO / VersityGW bucket + ConfigMap\n\nRead the endpoint, bucket, and credentials from a ConfigMap/Secret; point them at MinIO or VersityGW."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "object-storage",
                "portability": "MinIO / VersityGW bucket + ConfigMap",
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD006",
              "name": "ProprietaryS3primitiveusage",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Proprietary S3 primitive usage"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Object access uses boto3 S3 primitives (get_object, put_object, list_objects_v2, generate_presigned_url) rather than an S3-compatible abstraction."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Wrap in the object-store interface; the S3 API is portable, the SDK is not.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** S3-compatible client factory\n\nWrap in the object-store interface; the S3 API is portable, the SDK is not."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "object-storage",
                "portability": "S3-compatible client factory",
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD007",
              "name": "arn:awsliteralinsource",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "arn:aws literal in source"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A literal arn:aws: ARN is embedded, fixing the resource to one AWS partition/account/region."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Externalise into configuration and use Crossplane-provisioned resources with generated names.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** Crossplane composite + ConfigMap\n\nExternalise into configuration and use Crossplane-provisioned resources with generated names."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "identity",
                "portability": "Crossplane composite + ConfigMap",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD008",
              "name": "AWSIAM/STSroleassumption",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AWS IAM / STS role assumption"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Code assumes an IAM role via STS, which depends on the AWS identity control plane."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use workload identity from Kubernetes ServiceAccount (SPIFFE/IRSA-equivalent) or a Vault-injected token.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** Kubernetes ServiceAccount + Workload Identity\n\nUse workload identity from Kubernetes ServiceAccount (SPIFFE/IRSA-equivalent) or a Vault-injected token."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "identity",
                "portability": "Kubernetes ServiceAccount + Workload Identity",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD009",
              "name": "Non-portableIAMpolicydocument",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Non-portable IAM policy document"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An IAM policy document grants access using AWS ARNs or aws: source conditions, which no on-premises cluster can evaluate."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Replace with Kubernetes RBAC and an S3-compatible access key scoped to a bucket.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** RBAC Role/RoleBinding + MinIO policy\n\nReplace with Kubernetes RBAC and an S3-compatible access key scoped to a bucket."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "identity",
                "portability": "RBAC Role/RoleBinding + MinIO policy",
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD010",
              "name": "AWSmessagingserviceusage",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AWS messaging service usage"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Code publishes or consumes via SQS/SNS/Kinesis/EventBridge, proprietary managed brokers."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Target NATS JetStream or Redpanda, both of which run air-gapped.",
                "markdown": "**Portable replacement:** NATS JetStream / Redpanda\n\nTarget NATS JetStream or Redpanda, both of which run air-gapped."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "messaging",
                "portability": "NATS JetStream / Redpanda",
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TPD011",
              "name": "AWSmanageddatabaseusage",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AWS managed database usage"
